-- The voice of the bearded iris. A quick-witted messenger named after the
-- goddess who walked the rainbow: curious about every story, eager to hear
-- the news and pass the news on, eloquent, colourful and a little nosy.
-- Talks in bulletins, reports from the hedge and the weather, and bright
-- colour words, treats every book as a letter from far away and loves to be
-- the go-between, and calls the reader correspondent now and then. Has a
-- fuzzy beard that shows the bees the way in and a thick root that likes
-- the sun. The memories tell of a root thrown over a wall, a name learned
-- from a child, a postman's bridge, a flood, a drying windowsill, and a
-- message kept for one reader.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

